    expectedAnswer: "Graph revision should match the algorithm to the graph property: BFS for unweighted shortest paths, DFS for exploration/components, Dijkstra for non-negative weighted shortest paths, topological sort for DAG ordering, and Union Find for incremental undirected connectivity.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Identify the revision pattern.\n\nStep 1 — Representative pattern: unweighted shortest path with BFS.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nfunction shortestPath(\n  graph: ReadonlyMap<string, readonly string[]>,\n  start: string,\n  target: string,\n): number {\n  const distance = new Map<string, number>([[start, 0]]);\n  const queue = [start];\n  let head = 0;\n\n  while (head < queue.length) {\n    const node = queue[head++]!;\n    const current = distance.get(node)!;\n\n    if (node === target) return current;\n\n    for (const next of graph.get(node) ?? []) {\n      if (!distance.has(next)) {\n        distance.set(next, current + 1);\n        queue.push(next);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return -1;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN alternative:\n```ts\nfunction shortestPathUsingQueue(\n  graph: ReadonlyMap<string, readonly string[]>,\n  start: string,\n  target: string,\n): number {\n  const queue: Array<[string, number]> = [[start, 0]];\n  const visited = new Set([start]);\n\n  while (queue.length > 0) {\n    const [node, distance] = queue.shift()!;\n\n    if (node === target) return distance;\n\n    for (const next of graph.get(node) ?? []) {\n      if (!visited.has(next)) {\n        visited.add(next);\n        queue.push([next, distance + 1]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return -1;\n}\n```\n\nExample:\nA→B→D and A→C→D → shortest A→D = 2.\n\nComplexity:\nHead-index BFS O(V + E).\nRepeated `shift()` can make queue operations expensive on large arrays.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nUse the pattern only when its assumptions and invariant hold; always explain complexity.",
