    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Identify the revision pattern.\n\nStep 1 — Representative pattern: climbing stairs with compressed DP.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nfunction climbStairs(n: number): number {\n  if (n <= 1) return 1;\n\n  let twoBack = 1;\n  let oneBack = 1;\n\n  for (let step = 2; step <= n; step++) {\n    const current = twoBack + oneBack;\n    twoBack = oneBack;\n    oneBack = current;\n  }\n\n  return oneBack;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN / table:\n```ts\nfunction climbStairsUsingTable(n: number): number {\n  if (n <= 1) return 1;\n\n  const dp = [1, 1];\n\n  for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n    dp.push(dp[i - 1]! + dp[i - 2]!);\n  }\n\n  return dp[n]!;\n}\n```\n\nExample:\nn=4 → 5 ways.\n\nComplexity:\nO(n) time.\nCompressed version O(1) auxiliary space; table uses O(n).\n\nPattern takeaway:\nWrite `dp[i]` in English before writing the recurrence.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nUse the pattern only when its assumptions and invariant hold; always explain complexity.",
